{
  "requirement": "When given `--path <crate-dir>` and no existing Habeas dev dependency, `habeas setup` MUST add that local crate as the dev dependency. Repeating setup MUST NOT add a duplicate Habeas dependency.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** `requirements.cli.setup_local_path` is implemented completely and tested. I found no unmarked implementation and no unspecified behaviour.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `src/main.rs` defines `Setup { #[arg(long, value_name = \"crate-dir\")] path: Option<PathBuf> }` and passes it to `setup::run`. The `Command` enum is marked `{impl}` for `requirements.cli.clap`, which requires clap to define and parse options. That carries out the parsing half of `--path <crate-dir>`.\n- `has_habeas_dev_dependency` (src/setup.rs:25-33) is marked `{impl}`. It reports an existing Habeas dev dependency only when `[dev-dependencies]` has a `habeas` entry.\n- In `run` (src/setup.rs:92-189), the block marked `{impl}` for this requirement runs `cargo add --dev habeas --manifest-path <Cargo.toml>` only when no dev dependency exists.\n- When `--path` is given, it appends `--path <canonicalized crate dir>`. So the local crate is added as the dev dependency, and a relative path is resolved against the invocation directory. A missing directory makes `canonicalize` fail, which aborts setup before the manifest is touched. A failed `cargo add` is reported as an error.\n- Repeating setup finds the existing `habeas` dev dependency and skips `cargo add`, so no duplicate is added.\n- The remaining statements in `run` belong to `setup`, `setup_css`, `setup_project` and similar requirements, and carry their own markers. I saw no unspecified behaviour attributed to this requirement.\n\n**Tests** (`tests/setup.rs`, all marked `{test}` for this requirement)\n- `local_path_setup_adds_exactly_that_crate_once` passes a relative `--path`. It asserts there is exactly one `habeas` entry across `dependencies`, `dev-dependencies` and `build-dependencies`. That entry is in `dev-dependencies`, and its path resolves to the given crate. A second run with the absolute path leaves `Cargo.toml` byte-identical.\n- `local_path_setup_keeps_an_existing_habeas_dev_dependency` starts with `habeas = \"0.1\"` already present. Running setup with `--path` leaves the manifest unchanged, which covers the \"no existing dependency\" condition.\n- `local_path_setup_rejects_a_missing_crate_directory` expects setup to fail and checks that `Cargo.toml` is unchanged and no `habeas` dependency was added.\n- `setup_is_repeatable` runs setup twice with `--path`. It checks that `[dev-dependencies]` contains a path-based `habeas` entry, and that the other configuration is not duplicated.\n- `habeas_dependencies` is a helper marked `{test}` for this requirement.\n- Together these cover adding the dependency, a relative path, idempotent repetition, an existing dependency, and a missing path.\n\n**Residual note:** the `path` argument on `Command::Setup` carries no explicit `setup_local_path` marker. It is covered by the `clap` requirement's `{impl}`, whose text covers option definition and parsing, so I do not count it as a gap.",
